cks://ospd.process-profiles.process-type"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note"},{"path":["implementsProfile"],"id":"https://geolabs.github.io/bblocks-process-profiles/def/implementsProfile","jsonld_type":"@id","description":"IRI of the nearest applicable profile this process specialises, in the generic-profiles register -- normally an Implementation Profile (generic-profiles.implementation-profile.*, OGC 14-065 WPS 2.0.2 \u00a77.5.3: standard data formats, still not one specific deployment's own choice), or a Generic Profile directly when no Implementation Profile exists yet. Optional: most processes have no standardised abstract counterpart at all. `processDescription` and `plan` (this entry's own concrete binding) are what further specialise it to one real, deployed process -- Implementation (instance level) in the same standard's terms.","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://ospd.process-profiles.process-type"],"effectiveId":"https://geolabs.github.io/bblocks-process-profiles/def/implementsProfile"},{"path":["hasStep"],"id":"https://geolabs.github.io/bblocks-process-profiles/def/hasStep","jsonld_type":"@id","description":"Process types of the steps of a Workflow.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ospd.process-profiles.process-type"],"effectiveId":"https://geolabs.github.io/bblocks-process-profiles/def/hasStep"},{"path":["correspondences"],"id":"@nest","description":"Proposed correspondences with openEO (decision D5: apart from the meaning of the type). The SKOS mapping properties stay on the type; `openeoEquivalence` states the level, including `none`.","required":true,"schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://ospd.process-profiles.process-type"],"effectiveId":"@nest"},{"path":["correspondences","exactMatch"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch","jsonld_type":"@id","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://ospd.process-profiles.process-type"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/